infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title cProfile vs py-spy: two contracts for the same question
  desc Deterministic in-process tracing vs out-of-process sampling
  compares
    - label cProfile (tracer)
      children
        - label In-process, every call
          desc C hook fires on every call and return — nothing missed
        - label 1.3-2x slowdown
          desc Fixed per-call tax inflates tiny hot functions most
        - label Blind inside C
          desc json.dumps or numpy = one opaque row, no breakdown
        - label Single-thread by default
          desc Worker threads run unprofiled unless each installs one
        - label Needs in-process install
          desc Must run in the target; a stuck process needs a restart
    - label py-spy (sampler)
      children
        - label Out-of-process, ~100x/s
          desc Reads target memory via ptrace, walks frame structs
        - label ~1% overhead
          desc Target paused microseconds per sample — production-safe
        - label C frames under --native
          desc Interleaves native frames the tracer can never see
        - label Attach by PID, no restart
          desc No code change; dump x-rays a stuck 0% CPU worker
        - label Statistical blind spot
          desc Rare 5 ms spikes may never be sampled — needs wall time
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
